# Docs workflow

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `docs/SPEC.md` | What the system is. RTM is §2. Locked decisions are §10. |
| `docs/PLAN.md` | Phases, tasks, definition of done. Checkboxes are the status. |
| `docs/DESIGN.md` | Physical schema, source-to-target mapping, data dictionary. Skeleton until Phase 2. |
| `docs/PROGRESS_LOG.md` | Newest journal entry is first. Update the "Trạng thái hiện tại" block every session. |

## Before a multi-file change

State a short plan that cites the PLAN task and the R-xx codes it covers. Do not start Phase 1 profiling, ETL, or DSS implementation during a docs-only request.

## After the change

1. Tick the matching PLAN checkbox only if the task's definition of done is actually met.
2. Update the RTM status in SPEC §2 for every R-xx you touched. Status marks: `☐` not started, `◐` in progress, `⏸` blocked on data, `☑` done.
3. If a table, column, grain, or mapping changed, update `docs/DESIGN.md` in the same session (`06-dw-modeling`).
4. Prepend one new journal entry to `docs/PROGRESS_LOG.md`. Do not edit older entries. Also refresh "Trạng thái hiện tại".

## Labels

- `[ĐỀ]` — written in the assignment PDF.
- `[SUY LUẬN]` — inferred by the team; not a published grading criterion.
- `[GIẢ ĐỊNH]` — not yet verified. Name the check (S1–S6 or G1–G6).

## Numbers

Do not write a row count, byte size, date range, or test result that did not come from a command you ran in this session (or from an output already pasted in `data/README.md` / `PROGRESS_LOG.md`). If you did not run it, write "not measured" instead of a number.

Do not fill DESIGN grain estimates or SPEC quality issues from memory. Profiling belongs to Phase 1.
